    },
    "message": "Check WorldState v5 ticks on the same Rust path as v6\n\nA v5 world is the world of a Scenario without resource_service, written\ntoday, not an old saved shape. The end-of-tick check and the entity rules\nnow take it: they differ from v6 only in the resource service (no service\nstate, slots, tasks or completions, both hydration levels 0, an optional\nledger, and water and meal points may use the ordinary queues). tick_plan\ngives no resource config without resource_service, and the entity rules\ntake a v6 world only with one and a v5 world only without.\n\nTests break each v5 rule, and run the shared breaks on v5 worlds, so a\nrule gated on v6 fails its v5 case. The metrics shadow now compares v5\nworlds too.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
